                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7992ce1e-3b87-4ee5-85c9-8dd8d31fde7f",
                        "source_entry_id": "494e8ec7-cc71-3d25-a5e7-2bc641919a8d",
                        "target_lang_word": "act of God",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "act of God",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbbd31a8-2adb-3265-ab50-f7cc815bf15f",
                                        "entry_id": "9fd73550-b797-3fb4-aa3d-490d4bfc0ac7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unforeseen occurrence beyond one's control, such as a natural disaster."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "514fe73d-b797-4db3-b9f0-f4fd11004883",
                                                "sense_id": "fbbd31a8-2adb-3265-ab50-f7cc815bf15f",
                                                "text": "They didn't get shot to death in hold-ups, strangled to death in rapes, stabbed to death in saloons, bludgeoned to death with axes by parents or children or die summarily by some other act of God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c38c3c7e-748f-470f-97d2-ff9cdf5bf853",
                                                "sense_id": "fbbd31a8-2adb-3265-ab50-f7cc815bf15f",
                                                "text": "The action of “The Discovery of Heaven” combines the emotional melodrama of a telenovela with a sequence of events that an insurance lawyer would call acts of God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7901749c-025d-4dcc-9d66-ce60f77f616b",
                                                "sense_id": "fbbd31a8-2adb-3265-ab50-f7cc815bf15f",
                                                "text": "Infrastructure failures tend to be treated like acts of God, but of course they aren't really."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "997a57cc-0b5e-360e-8bbb-ebe7e0997247",
                                        "entry_id": "9fd73550-b797-3fb4-aa3d-490d4bfc0ac7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see act, of, God."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3f6cea6-a68c-4258-a066-047229dc4607",
                        "source_entry_id": "494e8ec7-cc71-3d25-a5e7-2bc641919a8d",
                        "target_lang_word": "force majeure",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "force majeure",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90da1c08-f3a3-33d9-8f14-8ad9e71c2e3d",
                                        "entry_id": "fb1628f9-dd65-3047-b027-5fb660413854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An overwhelming force."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93db51c5-3a66-4aff-ac27-51ab34e27ae6",
                                                "sense_id": "90da1c08-f3a3-33d9-8f14-8ad9e71c2e3d",
                                                "text": "They [children] realize their oughts no less sharply than their crosses; and this even though they are midgets in a land of giants who have forgotten much of their language and whose right is often founded solely on force majeure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e7cbf66-0f67-4c7c-a9a6-ff8341a624b6",
                                                "sense_id": "90da1c08-f3a3-33d9-8f14-8ad9e71c2e3d",
                                                "text": "Gen Y is a \"force majeure\" that will determine the future of the housing market. They are looking for housing solutions that cater to their mobile- and technology-focused lifestyles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9703d68-004d-37be-8cf0-ea07a10de334",
                                        "entry_id": "fb1628f9-dd65-3047-b027-5fb660413854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unavoidable circumstance, especially one that prevents someone from fulfilling a legal (usually contractual) obligation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3113cda8-bd53-4495-8f7a-87a025bda3c5",
                                                "sense_id": "d9703d68-004d-37be-8cf0-ea07a10de334",
                                                "text": "Brazil's largest trader of sugar and ethanol declared force majeure to some third party exporters of sugar with contracts to ship through its Santos Port terminal that burned down on Friday, sources in the sugar trade said."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d748b686-d6a5-4f2c-919f-db4358ed4c9d",
                                                "sense_id": "d9703d68-004d-37be-8cf0-ea07a10de334",
                                                "text": "18. GNM [Guardian News & Media Limited] shall not be liable for any failure to comply with its obligations where the failure is caused by something outside its reasonable control. Such circumstances shall include, but not be limited to, weather conditions, fire, flood, hurricane, strike, industrial dispute, war, hostilities, political unrest, riots, civil commotion, inevitable accidents, supervening legislation or any other circumstances amounting to force majeure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8955273-fd8b-4ef8-978c-dadf870467e3",
                                                "sense_id": "d9703d68-004d-37be-8cf0-ea07a10de334",
                                                "text": "Dated 14 July, the letter from the Russian state gas monopoly said it was declaring force majeure on supplies, starting from 14 June. Known as an \"act of God\" clause, a force majeure clause is standard in business contracts and spells out extreme circumstances that excuse a party from their legal obligations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
